==German==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|de|gmh|salz}}, from {{inh|de|goh|salz}} (akin to {{cog|osx|salt}}, {{cog|odt|salt}}, {{cog|ang|sealt}}, {{cog|non|salt}}), from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*salt}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*saltą}}, from {{inh|de|ine-pro|*seh₂l-|*séh₂l-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*séh₂ls}}. Compare {{cog|nl|zout}}, {{cog|en|salt}}, {{cog|da|salt}}. The Internet slang sense is a {{calque|de|en|salt|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/zalt͡s/|/zals/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Salz.ogg|audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|alts|als}}

